1
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:24,950
Hey, Phoebe.

2
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:24,950
Hey, tell me what you think.

3
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:28,750
The house next door to the one that we're buying just went on the market.

4
00:03:28,910 --> 00:03:31,210
I wanna take a look at it, but Chandler doesn't.

5
00:03:31,370 --> 00:03:32,540
We close escrow tomorrow.

6
00:03:32,710 --> 00:03:35,750
Seeing another house can only confuse us. We're easily confused.

7
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:37,380
We're not very bright.

8
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:41,550
But what if it's better than ours? Shouldn't we look?

9
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:43,090
What do you think, Pheebs?

10
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:47,430
Well, I think that shirt makes you look like you should work at a Baskin-Robbins.

11
00:03:51,230 --> 00:03:53,060
Anyway...

12
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:58,230
Hey, isn't Joey's agent Estelle Leonard?

13
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:58,230
Yeah.

14
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:00,030
She died.

15
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:00,030
You're kidding.

16
00:04:00,190 --> 00:04:02,660
That's terrible.

17
00:04:00,190 --> 00:04:02,660
Yeah, last Saturday.

18
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:07,410
Wow! She was the first black man to fly solo across the Atlantic.

19
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:13,580
Oh, wait a minute, I read the wrong one.

20
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:13,580
Oh, yeah?

21
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:18,090
Yeah, she was just an agent.

22
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:18,090
Joey's gonna be so upset.

23
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:22,680
I know. He always wanted to be the first black man to cross the Atlantic.

24
00:04:24,130 --> 00:04:25,760
We cannot tell Joey about this.

25
00:04:25,930 --> 00:04:28,560
He's already flipping out about everything that's changing.

26
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:30,520
This will push him over the edge.

27
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:33,310
You don't think we should tell him?

28
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:33,310
Not for a while.

29
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:36,480
Let's just give him a few days to get used to everything else.

30
00:04:36,650 --> 00:04:38,020
What if he reads it in the paper?

31
00:04:38,190 --> 00:04:41,820
Unless Snoopy says it to Charlie Brown, I think we're okay.

32
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:51,750
May I help you?

33
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:51,750
Yeah. I'm a friend of Rachel Green's.

34
00:04:51,910 --> 00:04:55,120
Um, actually, we met at the Christmas party about two years ago.

35
00:04:55,290 --> 00:04:58,590
Oh, right. Don?

36
00:04:55,290 --> 00:04:58,590
Close. Ron.

37
00:05:01,130 --> 00:05:03,090
Well, what can I do for you?

38
00:05:03,260 --> 00:05:07,970
Um, well, I'm here to see if you'll give Rachel her job back.

39
00:05:08,430 --> 00:05:11,220
Ah, did she ask you to come here and do this?

40
00:05:11,390 --> 00:05:13,100
No. First I have to get you to agree...

41
00:05:13,270 --> 00:05:16,060
...then we'll see if she wants to come back.

42
00:05:16,980 --> 00:05:18,980
Wow, that is tempting.

43
00:05:19,650 --> 00:05:24,400
She loved her job here. Let's face it you're not gonna find anyone...

44
00:05:24,570 --> 00:05:27,030
...who did it as well as she did. Isn't that true?

45
00:05:27,530 --> 00:05:31,240
She is good.

46
00:05:27,530 --> 00:05:31,240
Huh. I took a shot there.

47
00:05:31,700 --> 00:05:34,120
But I'm sorry, there's nothing I can do.

48
00:05:34,410 --> 00:05:38,040
Oh, that's not true. There's nothing I want to do.

49
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:40,710
I see.

50
00:05:41,460 --> 00:05:43,800
Thanks very much.

51
00:05:41,460 --> 00:05:43,800
Mm-hm.

52
00:05:48,140 --> 00:05:50,930
Is this your son?

53
00:05:48,140 --> 00:05:50,930
Yeah, his name is Ross.

54
00:05:55,600 --> 00:06:00,730
What?

55
00:05:55,600 --> 00:06:00,730
Nothing, it's just that it's close to Ron.

56
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:06,360
Does he, um...? Does little Ross like dinosaurs, by any chance?

57
00:06:06,530 --> 00:06:09,320
Yeah, they're all he talks about. Why?

58
00:06:10,030 --> 00:06:14,870
How would he like to come with me to the Museum of Natural History...

59
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:18,750
...after everyone else has left, just the two of us...

60
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:21,710
...and he can touch anything he wants?

61
00:06:27,170 --> 00:06:30,550
I just heard it how you must have heard it, and that's not good.

62
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:33,060
Let me start again. I'm a paleontologist.

63
00:06:33,220 --> 00:06:39,140
You'll be there with us, and the touching refers only to bones... Fossils!

64
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:46,940
You could really arrange that?

65
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:46,940
You let Rachel come back and it's done.

66
00:06:47,110 --> 00:06:50,860
Well, I guess having Rachel back wouldn't be the worst thing in the world.

67
00:06:51,030 --> 00:06:53,780
Yes! Thank you! This is great! Thank you so much.

68
00:06:53,950 --> 00:06:56,540
I swear, your kid's gonna have the time of his life.

69
00:06:56,700 --> 00:06:58,710
That's great. I worry about little Ross.

70
00:06:58,870 --> 00:07:02,330
He's always reading, collecting rocks and he's obsessed with dinosaurs.

71
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:03,630
He'll be fine!

72
00:07:06,420 --> 00:07:08,630
Hey, Pheebs.

73
00:07:06,420 --> 00:07:08,630
Hey.

74
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:11,680
Everything okay?

75
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:11,680
I'm just mad at my agent.

76
00:07:11,840 --> 00:07:13,470
Estelle? Why?

77
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:16,810
There's a part in this TV movie that I would be perfect for...

78
00:07:16,970 --> 00:07:20,140
...and I didn't even get put up for it. She better have a good reason.

79
00:07:21,940 --> 00:07:23,860
I'm guessing she does.

80
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:27,730
Well, I wanna hear it, because she keeps doing this.

81
00:07:27,900 --> 00:07:30,860
No, wait, wait, wait! All right, I gotta go.

82
00:07:31,030 --> 00:07:35,450
Just listen. Promise me that you will wait a minute before you call her.

83
00:07:35,620 --> 00:07:37,370
Well, Okay. Why?

84
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:43,420
Because a promise between friends means never having to give a reason.

85
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:50,050
I love that saying!

86
00:07:57,760 --> 00:08:01,390
Hello?

87
00:07:57,760 --> 00:08:01,390
Joey, it's Estelle.

88
00:08:02,230 --> 00:08:04,690
I was just gonna call you. That's weird.

89
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:08,570
It's a little coincidental, but believable.

90
00:08:10,320 --> 00:08:13,530
Listen, I'm sure you're wondering why I didn't get you...

91
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:15,990
...an audition for that TV movie.

92
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:17,450
Yeah, actually I am.

93
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:21,790
I guess I dropped the ball there. Whoopsie!

94
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:26,420
That's it? You know, it seems like all you do lately is drop the ball.

95
00:08:26,590 --> 00:08:29,630
Don't take that tone with me. Who do you think you are?

96
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:35,090
Alan Lemon, the first black man to fly solo across the Atlantic?

97
00:08:36,890 --> 00:08:39,350
No, look, all I'm saying is you're my agent...

98
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:42,520
...and you're not getting me any auditions and I'm tired of it.

99
00:08:42,680 --> 00:08:43,810
What are you saying?

100
00:08:43,980 --> 00:08:47,810
I'm saying that this isn't working for me anymore, okay, Estelle?

101
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:49,690
You're fired. Goodbye.

102
00:08:52,610 --> 00:08:54,780
Man, tough week for Estelle.

103
00:08:58,370 --> 00:09:00,200
Hi.

104
00:08:58,370 --> 00:09:00,200
Hi.

105
00:09:00,370 --> 00:09:02,830
Um, Emma left her stuffed T. rex at my house.

106
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:07,790
You know she can't sleep without it.

107
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:07,790
Ah. Well, she's asleep now.

108
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:11,210
Stop forcing that thing on her.

109
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:11,210
Okay.

110
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:13,970
Oh! You're not gonna believe what happened to me today!

111
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:17,260
Ralph Lauren called and gave me my job back.

112
00:09:17,430 --> 00:09:21,560
No!

113
00:09:17,430 --> 00:09:21,560
I mean, it was the weirdest thing.

114
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:24,810
They fire me and then out of nowhere, they just hire me back.

115
00:09:24,980 --> 00:09:27,900
I mean, that place must just be falling apart without me!

116
00:09:28,110 --> 00:09:31,480
So you're not going to Paris?

117
00:09:28,110 --> 00:09:31,480
No, I'm still going.

118
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:37,410
What?

119
00:09:37,570 --> 00:09:40,580
Well, when the Louis Vuitton people found out...

120
00:09:40,740 --> 00:09:44,330
...that Ralph Lauren wanted me back, they offered me more money!

121
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:47,000
Ross, isn't that great?

122
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:49,670
Yay!

123
00:09:56,010 --> 00:09:58,140
Hi. We're buying the house next door...

124
00:09:58,300 --> 00:10:00,510
...and we were wondering if we could take a look around?

125
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:03,520
I'm showing it to someone else, but please, look around.

126
00:10:03,680 --> 00:10:04,730
Thanks.

127
00:10:04,890 --> 00:10:07,230
I feel like we're cheating on our house.

128
00:10:07,730 --> 00:10:10,560
If we're gonna cheat, shouldn't it be with a hot, younger house...

129
00:10:10,730 --> 00:10:13,320
...that does stuff that our house won't do?

130
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:18,200
Ours is so much better.

131
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:22,240
This living room is smaller, the dining room looks like a cave.

132
00:10:22,410 --> 00:10:23,700
What a hole!

133
00:10:23,910 --> 00:10:27,660
So, what do you think?

134
00:10:23,910 --> 00:10:27,660
Loveit

135
00:10:27,910 --> 00:10:31,670
We already have one offer. I think the lady upstairs is gonna make another one.

136
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,800
They could be our neighbors. What are they like?

137
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:37,050
The woman upstairs is nice. She and her husband have two kids.

138
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:42,930
Uh, he's on Wall Street, and she's a...

139
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:42,930
Oh, my God!

140
00:10:52,650 --> 00:10:54,230
Sure.

141
00:10:59,860 --> 00:11:02,120
Hey, Joey, you wanna come with me to...?

142
00:11:02,700 --> 00:11:03,950
Are you okay?

143
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:07,290
Yeah, I just feel bad about firing Estelle.

144
00:11:07,450 --> 00:11:09,870
This has gotta be killing her.

145
00:11:12,830 --> 00:11:15,210
No, that wouldn't kill her.

146
00:11:15,380 --> 00:11:17,760
A coronary embolism might.

147
00:11:18,090 --> 00:11:21,800
I don't know. She's gotta be taking it hard. I was, like, her only client.

148
00:11:21,970 --> 00:11:24,100
Except for this guy who eats paper.

149
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:26,470
And I'm guessing he eats more money than he makes.

150
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:31,400
Look, I know she's not a great agent, but she did stick with me for 10 years.

151
00:11:33,060 --> 00:11:36,780
I'm gonna call her and hire her again.

152
00:11:33,060 --> 00:11:36,780
No, no, no! Don't call her.

153
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:40,650
You wait for her to call you.

154
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:40,650
Why?

155
00:11:41,070 --> 00:11:45,700
Because patience is the road to understanding.

156
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:50,620
Which is the key to a happy heart.

157
00:11:52,870 --> 00:11:55,460
You blow me away.

158
00:11:55,630 --> 00:11:58,590
All right, so promise you're gonna wait for her to call you?

159
00:11:58,760 --> 00:11:59,970
I promise.

160
00:11:58,760 --> 00:11:59,970
Okay.

161
00:12:00,130 --> 00:12:04,390
And that means never having to give a reason.

162
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:10,480
What a small world!

163
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:13,730
And yet I never run into Beyoncé.

164
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:16,900
You two know each other?

165
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:20,360
Oh, we go way back. Before Monica made an honest man out of him...

166
00:12:20,530 --> 00:12:23,200
...Chandler used to be my little love muffin.

167
00:12:25,780 --> 00:12:28,950
So are you guys thinking of getting this house too?

168
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:32,790
Are we gonna have a bidding war? I better warn you, I'm a toughie.

169
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:34,790
Don't. Don't. Don't.

170
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:37,420
No, actually, we are buying the house next door.

171
00:12:38,250 --> 00:12:39,920
Why?

172
00:12:42,590 --> 00:12:44,630
I don't know why.

173
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:48,310
Oh, that decides it, then! I was on the fence.

174
00:12:48,470 --> 00:12:51,100
But knowing that you two would be our neighbors?

175
00:12:51,270 --> 00:12:53,480
Now we have to get it.

176
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:55,770
Ellen, we're gonna talk numbers.

177
00:13:00,690 --> 00:13:02,900
This cannot be happening.

178
00:13:03,070 --> 00:13:05,530
Okay, the realtor said another couple made an offer.

179
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:10,370
Maybe the Janices won't get it! Maybe the other couple will.

180
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:15,000
The only way that that is going to happen is if the other couple are the Hitlers!

181
00:13:17,750 --> 00:13:20,670
Okay, okay! All right, what if we get both houses?

182
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:24,050
We can turn this one into a guesthouse!

183
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:24,050
That's a great idea!

184
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:26,640
By the way, I don't mean to sound distasteful...

185
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:29,050
...but when did you start crapping money?

186
00:13:30,430 --> 00:13:32,470
You come up with an idea.

187
00:13:30,430 --> 00:13:32,470
All right.

188
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:36,060
We've still got three hours till escrow closes on our house.

189
00:13:36,230 --> 00:13:38,440
We can still get out.

190
00:13:36,230 --> 00:13:38,440
But we love our house.

191
00:13:38,610 --> 00:13:40,610
Will we love it so much with her next door?

192
00:13:40,770 --> 00:13:42,860
And she's gonna be louder out here too!

193
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:46,490
Just the crickets and, "Oh, my God!"

194
00:13:47,280 --> 00:13:51,030
Okay. But if we don't get this house, she's still gonna show up wherever we go.

195
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:54,290
At least if she's here, it eliminates the element of surprise.

196
00:13:54,450 --> 00:13:56,960
Never again will you have to hear the three words...

197
00:13:57,120 --> 00:14:00,210
...that make your balls jump back up inside your body!

198
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:09,220
Well, we have to do something. We can't have her living next door.

199
00:14:13,680 --> 00:14:15,930
Oh, that does it too.

200
00:14:22,980 --> 00:14:24,230
Who is it?

201
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:26,030
It's me. Ron.

202
00:14:27,610 --> 00:14:30,450
Look, I know Rachel turned you down...

203
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:34,540
...but I think there's a way you might be able to get her to come back.

204
00:14:34,700 --> 00:14:40,960
This may surprise you, but rehiring fired employees is not my main job.

205
00:14:41,330 --> 00:14:42,840
Just hear me out.

206
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:47,300
How would you feel about offering her a raise?

207
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:53,560
Not good, Ron.

208
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:56,890
Perhaps I can persuade you.

209
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:59,730
What if you could give your son...

210
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:05,690
...this genuine pterodactyl egg replica.

211
00:15:12,410 --> 00:15:14,990
Wow. That's pretty cool.

212
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:18,660
Huh? So? Do we have a deal?

213
00:15:19,290 --> 00:15:22,460
Qkay, you got it.

214
00:15:19,290 --> 00:15:22,460
Yes! Yes!

215
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:25,750
This is gonna make me very popular.

216
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:25,750
Oh.

217
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:28,210
Believe me, the ladies, they love it.

218
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:35,010
I meant with my son.

219
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:37,600
Good, because the ladies, not so much.

220
00:15:45,770 --> 00:15:48,740
Joey, this is AI Zebooker...

221
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:51,070
...the guy who eats paper.

222
00:15:51,530 --> 00:15:54,530
I'm sure you've heard that Estelle passed away.

223
00:15:54,700 --> 00:15:57,330
I wanted to let you know there's a memorial for her...

224
00:15:57,490 --> 00:16:01,040
...at the Westside Chapel tomorrow at 10.

225
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:03,040
Hope you can make it.

226
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Oh, my God.

227
00:16:14,180 --> 00:16:17,760
Hello?

228
00:16:14,180 --> 00:16:17,760
Joey, it's Estelle.

229
00:16:23,230 --> 00:16:24,770
Estelle?

230
00:16:24,940 --> 00:16:30,320
Yeah, I wanted to call and tell you that there's no hard feelings for firing me.

231
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:39,040
Okay. I just... I can't believe you're calling me.

232
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:41,200
I didn't think I should just drop by.

233
00:16:41,370 --> 00:16:44,250
No, no! Don't drop by! Don't drop by!

234
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:45,710
No.No.No.

235
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:50,170
Anyway, you did what you had to do. I'm okay.

236
00:16:50,340 --> 00:16:52,920
Can I ask you something? Um...

237
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:55,220
What's it like there?

238
00:16:56,510 --> 00:16:57,970
It's all right.

239
00:16:59,140 --> 00:17:01,140
Look, kiddo, I gotta go.

240
00:17:01,310 --> 00:17:04,560
Good luck with the career. You're gonna be huge!

241
00:17:04,730 --> 00:17:08,360
Thanks for everything, Estelle. Bye.

242
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:13,530
"Out of area." Boy, I'll say.

243
00:17:17,570 --> 00:17:21,240
Well, I just talked to Sid.

244
00:17:21,410 --> 00:17:24,040
We are definitely putting in an offer on the house.

245
00:17:24,210 --> 00:17:26,170
And I'll bet we get it!

246
00:17:26,330 --> 00:17:29,170
The Hitlers will be so disappointed.

247
00:17:30,250 --> 00:17:34,670
All right, I gotta run. Tell Monica I say goodbye.

248
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:37,550
And I'll see you later, neighbor. Ha, ha.

249
00:17:38,010 --> 00:17:39,600
Wait!

250
00:17:40,390 --> 00:17:44,770
I just want you to know that I'm so happy you're going to be here.

251
00:17:44,930 --> 00:17:47,060
Oh, me too.

252
00:17:47,230 --> 00:17:48,980
Because...

253
00:17:49,150 --> 00:17:51,020
...that way...

254
00:17:51,230 --> 00:17:54,490
...we can pick up where we left off.

255
00:17:57,950 --> 00:18:01,280
Huh?

256
00:17:57,950 --> 00:18:01,280
I never stopped loving you.

257
00:18:01,450 --> 00:18:04,290
Oh, my...

258
00:18:01,450 --> 00:18:04,290
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

259
00:18:06,750 --> 00:18:09,000
I want you.

260
00:18:09,170 --> 00:18:10,880
I need you.

